## 3. Architecture overview

```
Widget (React)
 ├─ Chat panel (existing)
 ├─ GuideEngine (state machine: idle → running → paused → completed/aborted)
 │    ├─ GuideRegistry client cache
 │    ├─ StepRunner (route changes, wait for element, validation, advance)
 │    ├─ TargetResolver (finds elements by data-guide-id, with fallbacks)
 │    ├─ Overlay (spotlight, dimmed backdrop, pointer arrow)
 │    ├─ Avatar3D (the existing 3D model, rendered with three.js) + movement controller
 │    ├─ VoiceController (TTS, optional voice commands)
 │    └─ CaptionBar + ControlBar (Next/Back/Repeat/Pause/Mute/Exit/Ask)
Backend
 ├─ Guide registry API (role-filtered guide definitions)
 ├─ Tool: start_guide / search_guides (called by the LLM)
 ├─ Progress + analytics endpoints
 └─ Optional TTS endpoint (fallback voice)
```

**Key principle:** the LLM only **chooses a guide by id** from the list the server allows for that user's role. The LLM never generates selectors, scripts or step content at runtime. Guides are authored, static, reviewed data. This keeps guides reliable and safe.

