## 4. Guide definitions (authored data)

Create a typed registry (JSON or TypeScript) and a Zod schema for validation:

```ts
interface GuideDef {
  guideId: string;                         // e.g. "students.import"
  title: { en: string; ml?: string };
  summary: { en: string; ml?: string };
  keywords: string[];                      // for search/matching ("import students", "upload excel", "add many students", ...)
  roles: Role[] | 'public';                // who may run it; 'public' = pre-login pages
  startRoute?: string;                     // where to begin if user is elsewhere
  steps: GuideStep[];
  completion: { message: { en: string; ml?: string }; followUpChips?: string[] };
}

interface GuideStep {
  stepId: string;
  route?: string | RegExp;                 // page this step lives on (engine navigates or instructs if different)
  target: {
    guideId: string;                       // value of data-guide-id on the element
    fallbacks?: string[];                  // alternative data-guide-ids / aria-labels / text matches
    scrollIntoView?: boolean;
  } | null;                                // null = informational step with no target
  instruction: { en: string; ml?: string }; // caption text (short, one action)
  voice?: { en: string; ml?: string };      // spoken text (defaults to instruction)
  action: 'click' | 'type' | 'select' | 'upload' | 'read' | 'wait';
  completeWhen?:                           // how the engine knows the user finished the step
    | { type: 'click' }                    // target clicked
    | { type: 'valueFilled'; minLength?: number; pattern?: string }   // input filled (never reads/stores the value)
    | { type: 'valueChanged' }             // select/checkbox changed
    | { type: 'fileSelected' }             // file input has a file
    | { type: 'routeChanged'; to: string | RegExp }
    | { type: 'elementAppears'; guideId: string }
    | { type: 'manual' };                  // user presses Next
  hint?: { en: string; ml?: string };       // shown after 15 s of no progress
  optional?: boolean;                      // can be skipped
  sensitive?: boolean;                     // true for password/OTP fields (Section 8)
}
```

Rules:
- **English is the default and required language** for every guide. Malayalam text is **optional** (`ml`): if a guide has Malayalam text and the user switches the assistant language to Malayalam, show/speak Malayalam; otherwise use English. Never block a guide because Malayalam is missing. One action per step, short sentences, plain words.
- Create guides for **every task listed in the audit** (Section 2.2), for the correct roles, including the two examples above. Each guide must be tested (Section 11).
- Registry lives server-side (`/guides/*.json` or TS), served by role. Public guides are served without authentication but are restricted to public pages (login, register, forgot password).

